{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 10.0% a year from $129,025 million in FY2017 to $303,154 million in FY2026 [F1][F10][F203]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The shape is a steady compounding line with two step-ups: revenue growth of 17.5% in FY2021 and 15.8% in FY2022 against 9.2% in FY2020 [D189][D238][D140]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2021's jump came from a 16% comparable sales increase, with e-commerce comparable sales up 44% and gasoline prices adding 100 basis points to net sales [P54][P55]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2022 followed on a 14% comparable sales increase, with the strongest growth in gasoline, business centers and travel, and sales still lifted by inflation [P42]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The US segment supplied most of the growth, contributing 6.2pp of FY2025's 8.2% and 7.2pp of FY2026's 10.1% revenue increase [D669][D385][D672][D434]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026's $27,335 million net sales increase was primarily a comparable sales gain of $22,457 million, or 8%, on 5% higher average ticket and 3% higher frequency [P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Food and Sundries remained the largest product line at 38.5% of FY2026 revenue but contributed only 2.6pp of growth, while warehouse ancillary and other businesses added 3.7pp [D558][D560][D601]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 12.3% a year against revenue's 10.0%, and operating costs grew 0.1pp slower than revenue in FY2026 [F204][F203][D458]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS compounded at 14.6% against net income's 14.7%, with the diluted share count essentially flat at 444.4 million [F207][F205][X100]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin reached 3.9% in FY2026, its window high, against a 3.4% median and a 3.1% low in FY2019 [F32][D691][D692][D690]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 margin rose 0.1pp, with SG&A adding 0.1pp and cost of revenue flat at 87.2% of revenue [D447][D460][D459][D413]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "SG&A fell 10 basis points as a share of net sales, though excluding gasoline price inflation it rose one basis point, with foreign currency adding $126 [P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2026 net margin of 3.0% sat 0.9pp below the 3.9% operating margin, a gap of 0.9pp [F52][F32][D448]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $15,817 million was 1.71x net income in FY2026, above the 0.99x window median, and free cash flow was 1.02x net income [F82][F42][D421][D701][D422]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2026 operating cash increase was primarily due to higher operating income and reduced net investment in merchandise inventories from faster turns and improved supplier payment terms [P6]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin was 3.1% against a 2.8% median, with capex at 2.1% of revenue and 2.41x D&A [D418][D698][D417][D423]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Investing outflow rose to $6,378 million from $5,311 million, primarily capital expenditures [F112][F111][P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net cash reached $15,139 million, or 5.0% of revenue, in FY2026 from $9,496 million a year earlier [D427][D428][D378]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net cash position ranked at the 100th percentile of six retail peers against a -4.4% median, and the current ratio was 1.06x versus a 1.02x median [D715][D716][F182][D704]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $3,306 million absorbed 35.2% of free cash flow, with $848 million of repurchases under the January 2023 program [D429][D430][X110][P3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Long-term debt fell 31.5% to $3,914 million while the diluted share count slipped 0.1% [D445][F192][D452]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 3.9% sits at the 17th percentile of six retail peers against a 5.0% median, and net margin of 3.0% also ranks 17th against 3.5% [F32][D709][D710][F52][D711][D712]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The thin-margin model is structural rather than deteriorating, since the margin is at its window high, but it leaves little cushion if merchandise costs or wages outrun sales."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow conversion of 1.02x net income ranked at the 67th percentile against a 0.83x median, and capex has risen to 2.41x D&A from 1.83x in FY2017 [D422][D717][D718][D423][D11]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Rising capital intensity is the item to watch: if capex keeps outpacing depreciation, the free cash flow that funds buybacks and dividends narrows."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether FY2027 operating margin holds at the FY2026 high of 3.9% or slips toward the 3.4% median, reported in the FY2027 10-K [F32][D692]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether free cash flow per dollar of net income stays above the 0.99x median or falls back toward the 0.60x FY2022 low, reported in the FY2027 10-K [D701][D699]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether net cash as a share of revenue holds above the FY2026 5.0% or reverses toward the FY2024 2.1%, reported in the FY2027 10-K [D428][D330]."}
  ]}
]}
